    "body": "Yep, even if that happed then step 5. will throw and 6. will never happend. Basically I try figuret out what is relation beetwen context and string, in this case context will be always document element for this parsed document? I see that when using some methods which operate on this algo browsers sometimes throw for passing string `\"<a></a><b></b>\"` (`createContextualFragment`) but not for `\"<a><b></b></a>\"` (`innerHTML/outerHTML/insertAdjacentHTML`) and still don't know why. So algo will parse `<context>string</context>` or just `string`?\n",
