    "updated_at": "2016-05-12T22:23:05Z",
    "body": "Hmm I forgot about comment in source, ok, now it's more clrear. But why this example not throw and print \"x\" in iframe (tested in Gecko)? The same is for xml file (without iframe) or when use `createDocument()`. Looks like bug in Gecko because Blink/Edge/IE11/Presto throw in external xhml file and Blink also throw for `createDocument()` in html file.\nTest for .xhtml:\n\n``` html\n<html xmlns='http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml'><foo--/>\n<script>/*<![CDATA[*/\n    var foo = document.documentElement.firstChild;\n    foo.innerHTML = 'x</foo--><!--y';\n    console.log(foo.innerHTML);\n/*]]>*/</script>\n</html>\n```\n\nTest for .html:\n\n``` html\n<html>\n<script>\n    var doc = document.implementation.createDocument(null, null, null);\n    var el = doc.createElementNS(\"\", \"root--\");\n    var str = \"a</root--><!--\";\n    el.innerHTML = str;\n    console.log(el.innerHTML);\n</script>\n</html>\n```\n\nUp: when we use `doc.createElementNS(\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\", \"root--\");` then also throw in Edge/IE11/Presto.\n",
